      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3b65cefe-3b99-5f4b-8779-fa82c41fbbed",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Isochrysis galbana\n- Concepts: Haptophytes, bivalve larvae, cosmetic and hair-growth properties\n- Chemicals: Isopropyl alcohol, propan-2-ol, dimethyl carbinol, hexane, ethyl acetate, ethanol, water, methanol, isopropanol\n\nFacts:\n- Isochrysis galbana is a species of haptophytes.\n- Isochrysis galbana is an outstanding food for various bivalve larvae.\n- Isochrysis galbana extract is said to have cosmetic and hair-growth properties when extracted with hexane, ethyl acetate, ethanol, water, methanol, or isopropanol.\n- Isopropyl alcohol has the IUPAC name propan-2-ol and is also called dimethyl carbinol.\n- Isopropyl alcohol is sometimes incorrectly called isopropanol.\n- Isopropyl alcohol has the chemical formula C3H8O, also written as CH3CHOHCH3 or (CH3)2CHOH and sometimes represented as i-PrOH.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
