        "text": "Page: Isochrysis galbana. Sentence: Isochrysis galbana is a species of haptophytes.\nPage: Isochrysis galbana. Sentence: It is an outstanding food for various bivalve larvae.\nPage: Isochrysis galbana. Sentence: The \"Isochrysis galbana\" extract is said to have certain cosmetic and hair-growth properties when using hexane, ethyl acetate, ethanol, water, methanol, or isopropanol as extractants.\nPage: Isopropyl alcohol. Sentence: Isopropyl alcohol (IUPAC name propan-2-ol), also called dimethyl carbinol or, incorrectly, isopropanol, is a compound with the chemical formula CHO or CHOH or CHCHOHCH (sometimes represented as \"i\"-PrOH).",
